@startuml
left to right direction

package "Presentation Layer" {
  [Angular 19 Frontend] as Frontend
}

package "Business Logic Layer" {
  [Spring Boot 3 Backend] as Backend
  () "Token Generation" as TokenGen
  () "Token Validation" as TokenVal
  () "Email Service" as EmailService

  Backend -- TokenGen
  Backend -- TokenVal
  Backend -- EmailService
}

package "Persistence Layer" {
  [PostgreSQL Database\n<<Docker>>] as Database
  [File Storage] as Storage
}

package "External Services" {
  [Keycloak\n<<Docker>>] as Keycloak
  [SMTP Server] as SMTP
}

Frontend --> Backend : REST/HTTP\n(Token requests,\nreport access)
Backend --> Database : JPA/JDBC/Hibernate\n(Transactional operations)
Backend --> Storage : File I/O\n(Report storage)
Backend --> Keycloak : OpenID Connect\n(Admin authentication)
Backend --> SMTP : SMTP Protocol\n(Notifications)

note right of Backend
  Handles:
  - Token management
  - Authentication integration
  - Business logic
  - Data persistence
end note

@enduml
